idate, with 3 tiles left, which is higher probability than W1 with 2 tiles left. Also, your hand is already all chows, so keeping B3 maintains the chance for \"All Simples\" (2 points) if you win with B3 pair, because W1 is a terminal and would break \"All Simples\". If you discard B3 and win with W1 pair, you would have a terminal in the pair, losing \"All Simples\". So discarding W1 preserves \"All Simples\" for extra points. Given the tile counts and scoring potential, discarding W1 is slightly better.\n\nAnswer: Play W1"}
